  "body": "Small findings of the post audit against the Mach3/Mach4 manuals (#4130). None changes a toolpath.\n\n1. Mach3: the sequence-number option allows a start up to 999999, and the numbers grow with no limit (`assets/posts/mach3.cps:42`, `:111-115`). Mach3 accepts N up to 99999. Cap the option and wrap or refuse past the limit.\n2. Mach3: the header writes no path-control mode (`mach3.cps:325`), so the program uses the `G61`/`G64` that the control had before. The Mach4 post writes `G64` (`mach4.cps:371`).\n3. Mach4: a smoothing request is stored and then not used (`mach4.cps:390-391`; `smoothTol` is not read again). The operator is not told. Mach3 writes a note (`mach3.cps:421-427`).\n\nEvidence: upstream/main `f0bdc5109`.\n\nDone means: each item is fixed with a test, or closed with a reason in a comment.\n",
